Author: loop-bench <loop-bench@localhost>
Date:   Sun Nov 15 22:41:25 2026 +0100

    fix(test): allow close handlers to complete before test teardown

    The test cleanup was terminating WebSocket clients but not waiting for
    their close handlers to execute. This caused logging to occur after Jest
    had marked the test as complete, triggering 'Cannot log after tests are
    done' errors. Add a 10ms delay after terminating clients to allow close
    handlers on the server side to fire and complete before proceeding with
    server shutdown.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

